% A directory self.glp's PARAMETERISED type is visible to that directory's other
% modules, exactly as a monomorphic one is (modules.tex sec:mod-design, "Implicit
% ancestor scoping": a module sees every type and procedure definition from every
% ancestor scope).  Para(C) below is named only by code.glp, which is a sibling
% module and not a descendant of anything but this directory.  GREEN.
%
% code.glp is SGSG's 2026-08-03 reproduction verbatim, so its line 5 — the line
% their report cites — is still line 5.  What that report measured was a program
% root OUTSIDE programs/, where Section S10 of the suite says there is no
% ancestor scope at all, so neither Para NOR Plain was in scope there.
Plain   ::= wrap(Constant).
Para(C) ::= wrap(C).
imported procedure code#plain(Stream(Plain)?).
exported procedure plain(Stream(Plain)?).
plain(X) :- code # plain(X?).
